      "size": [
        460,
        520
      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 22,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "Note: MOSS-Image",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## MOSS-Image\n\nSettings from the MOSS prompting study: 20 steps, CFG 5, euler / sgm_uniform, SLG (uncond skip, layer 22, 0-1), empty negative, 1344x768. Prompt: prose, one sentence per element, no quality prefix.\n\nRTX 5070 Laptop: plain 23 s, Automatic (3 stages, \u0394 0.05) 18 s, Manual (0.5x to step 10) 15 s.\n\n## SPEED on an image model\n\nAll SPEED nodes here have **model_type = image**. The sampler input comes from KSamplerSelect (euler).\n\n1. **Harvest** (muted): unmute it, run once, and read the report. Paste `noise_amplitude` and\n   `noise_decay_exponent` into the Automatic node. The values already in it were harvested from this\n   prompt and seed on an RTX 5070 Laptop.\n2. **SPEED Automatic** (active): stage boundaries come from the Harvest fit and `Tolerance (Delta)`.\n   At \u0394 0.005 the low-resolution stage ends in the first steps, so it saves little; \u0394 0.05 is the\n   useful setting for images.\n3. **SPEED Manual** (muted): fixed boundary, half resolution to step 10, then full resolution.\n   Unmute it and mute Automatic to use it instead.\n\n**Plain reference** (muted) is the same graph on SamplerCustomAdvanced, for comparison.\nSPEED changes the composition at a given seed (the low-resolution stage gets its own noise), so compare\nlooks, not pixels.\n"
      ],
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    }
  ],
